<title>USA: PacifiCorp Bridger units back on line.</title>
<headline>PacifiCorp Bridger units back on line.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Two 550 MW coal-fired units at the Jim Bridger coal-fired power plant in Wyoming were restarted over the weekend, sources familiar with the plant's operations said Monday.</p>
<p>Unit 3 had been down for a week due to trouble with a boiler valve, while unit 2 tripped off early Friday morning because of a leak.</p>
<p>Bridger's other two 550 MW units were also said to be operating at full rates.</p>
<p>PacifiCorp is the majority owner and operator of the Bridger units.</p>
<p>--Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
</text>
